      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the probability that the two-digit number \\(ab\\) (where \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are the digits obtained from rolling two fair 6-sided dice) and both \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are divisible by 3, we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the possible values for \\(a\\) and \\(b\\).\n2. Determine which of these values are divisible by 3.\n3. Calculate the probability.\n\nFirst, let's identify the possible values for \\(a\\) and \\(b\\). Since a die has 6 faces, the possible values for \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are the integers from 1 to 6.\n\nNext, we need to identify which of these values are divisible by 3. The numbers divisible by 3 in the range from 1 to 6 are 3 and 6.\n\nSo, the possible values for \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) that are divisible by 3 are 3 and 6. Therefore, the pairs \\((a, b)\\) that satisfy this condition are \\((3, 3)\\), \\((3, 6)\\), \\((6, 3)\\), and \\((6, 6)\\).\n\nThere are 4 favorable outcomes.\n\nNow, we need to determine the total number of possible outcomes when rolling two 6-sided dice. Each die has 6 faces, so the total number of outcomes is:\n\\[6 \\times 6 = 36.\\]\n\nThe probability that the two-digit number \\(ab\\) and both \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are divisible by 3 is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of possible outcomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{4}{36} = \\frac{1}{9}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the probability is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{9}}\\).",
